{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a7f19b4f7e4dd5c5","name":"Maris Brood","source":{"id":"source:reference-a7f19b4f7e4dd5c5","title":"Maris Brood","revision":19517,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:06:54Z","sha256":"2c6ae60c08ae2018844b49e782806627ed048268266ef949d11a70400869662b","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19517","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Maris%20Brood&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a7f19b4f7e4dd5c5","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Felucian Shamans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Felucian_Shamans","referenceId":"reference:3f5a6e0e902bd292"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The last Padawan of Jedi Master ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shaak Ti"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shaak_Ti","referenceId":"reference:7d8b4c369f966b9d"},", Maris Brood fled to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Felucia"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Felucia","referenceId":"reference:250a80750f084438"}," after serving the Republic during the later years of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," and escaping the execution of Order 66. During her time on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Felucia"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Felucia","referenceId":"reference:250a80750f084438"},"- while her Master focused on training the native shamans in the ways of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},"- Brood wandered off on her own, testing her skills against the planet's hostile wildlife and exploring ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," along her own course.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["After Vader's minion defeats ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shaak Ti"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shaak_Ti","referenceId":"reference:7d8b4c369f966b9d"},", Brood is left on her own with the Force-sensitive natives and the harsh Felucian wilderness. Fueled by her anger at ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shaak Ti"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shaak_Ti","referenceId":"reference:7d8b4c369f966b9d"}," for abandoning her, horror at the carnage of her Master's death, and isolation on the dangerous planet of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Felucia"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Felucia","referenceId":"reference:250a80750f084438"},", Brood descends toward ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},". She continues training ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Felucian Shamans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Felucian_Shamans","referenceId":"reference:3f5a6e0e902bd292"}," in the Jedi arts but, colored by her rage, corrupts many of them into turning to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},". Brood establishes herself as the leader of the dark Felucian shamans and trains many ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rancors"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rancors"}," to do her bidding. Her most dangerous ally is the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Bull Rancor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bull_Rancor","referenceId":"reference:42d38780e590a875"},", which she uses to fend off any intruders into her domain.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Maris Brood Statistics (CL 7)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Zabrak"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Zabrak","referenceId":"reference:c2636ff18986b258"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId